{title: Move it on over}
{artist: Hank Williams}
{key: E}
{tempo: 165}
{comment: Chart adapted from public chord sheets — key E shuffle}

{start_of_verse}
[E]Came in last night at half past ten
That baby of mine wouldn't let me in
So [A]move it on over, move it on over
[E]Move it on over, move it on over
Move over little dog 'cause the [B7]big dog's moving [E]in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[E]She's changed the lock on my front door
My door key don't fit no more
So [A]get it on over, move it on over
[E]Scoot it on over, move it on over
Move over skinny dog 'cause the [B7]fat dog's moving [E]in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[E]This doghouse here is mighty small
But it's better than no house at all
So [A]ease it on over, move it on over
[E]Drag it on over, move it on over
Move over old dog 'cause a [B7]new dog's moving [E]in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_instrumental: break}
|E| |E| |A| |E| |B7| |E|
{end_of_instrumental}

{start_of_verse}
[E]She told me not to play around
But I done let the deal go down
So [A]pack it on over, move it on over
[E]Tote it on over, move it on over
Move over nice dog 'cause a [B7]mad dog's moving [E]in
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
[E]She warned me once, she warned me twice
But I don't take no one's advice
So [A]scratch it on over, move it on over
[E]Shake it on over, move it on over
Move over short dog 'cause a [B7]tall dog's moving [E]in
{end_of_verse}
